WEB SOURCE (the specification) — components/forms/UnitInput.tsx
  A controlled, settings-aware number-with-unit field. It stores its value in TeslaSync's canonical
  metric (distance → miles, speed → mph, temperature → °C, energy → kWh, percent → 0..100, currency →
  as-typed), renders it in the user's preferred DISPLAY unit derived from useSettings() on every
  render, parses user-typed text on blur / Enter, and re-syncs the field when the unit preference
  changes WITHOUT clobbering text the user is currently typing (the resync only happens when the
  input is not focused). Props: value (number|null canonical), onChange(next), unit (UnitKind),
  parseStrict?, and the forwarded <Input> props (label, …). Data source: useSettings. Shared
  components: @/components/ui (<Input>). Charts/maps: none.
  Behaviour ported verbatim (lib/unitInput.ts):
    • formatForUnit  : nil/non-finite → ""; canonical→display (km = miles*1.609344; °F = °C*9/5+32);
      Intl.NumberFormat minFrac 0 / maxFrac max(0,decimal_precision) / useGrouping=false. (Swift
      NumberFormatter + roundingMode .halfUp to match Intl's half-away-from-zero.)
    • parseForUnit   : trim; for currency strip the settings symbol + accounting parens ("($10)"→-10);
      for percent strip a trailing "%"; strip the longest trailing unit suffix (km/h, kwh, mph, °c,
      °f, kw, mi, km, ° — longest-first, case-insensitive); strict → plain Double() else
      parseLocaleNumber; display→canonical (km miles / °F → °C). Empty/unparseable → nil.
    • parseLocaleNumber : locale group separator removed (when distinct from the decimal), decimal
      normalised to "." ('1,234.56' en-US, '1.234,56' de-DE → 1234.56).
    • unitSymbol     : distance mi/km · speed mph/(km/h) · temperature °C/°F · energy kWh · percent %
      · currency settings.currency_symbol (fallback "$"). Shown as the trailing field suffix.
  i18n keys extracted from source: the documented canonical label "Battery Capacity"
  (t('chargePlanner.batteryCapacity', 'Battery Capacity')). The remaining native strings are P4 leaf
  chrome (prompt / not-set / loading / error / freshness / a11y), all via the P1/S10 facade.
  P4 leaf states: the web field has a settings data source, so the surface reproduces loading / ready
  (empty + populated — never a blank box) / error (QueryError peer) + the orthogonal connectivity
  axis (stale chip + one-shot auto-refresh; offline chip over the cached value). Each has a #if DEBUG
  preview + a unit test.

